{
  "title": "Upgrade default AI models (still google/gemini-2.5-flash from mid-2025) with an eval to pick replacements",
  "description": "ramekin-core/src/ai/config.rs defaults every text feature to google/gemini-2.5-flash and images to google/gemini-2.5-flash-image. \
Prod (~/code/ramekin dev.env/cli.env) doesn't set RAMEKIN_AI_MODEL, so prod runs all AI features on those defaults: text/photo extraction, auto-tag, custom enrich, title normalization, description generation, photo generation. cli.env.example still lists openai/gpt-4.1-mini and anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6 as alternatives, which are also stale.\n\
\n\
Tasks:\n\
1. \
Check OpenRouter's current catalog (don't rely on training data) for current fast/cheap and frontier models, including pricing and JSON-mode support.\n\
2. \
Consider per-feature models rather than one global model. \
Extraction (text/photo) and ingredient resolution reward accuracy; tagging and descriptions can use the cheapest good model.\n\
3. \
Compare candidates with the existing cached harnesses (make title-normalization-test, make description-generation-test) plus the text-import eval from p2-text-import-structured-ingredients, and record results in the PR. \
These are text-only, but the text model also serves the multimodal request in ramekin-core/src/ai/photo_extract.rs, and the image model serves recipe-photo generation (generate_recipe_photo.rs). \
Before changing either default, confirm on OpenRouter that the candidate supports image input (text model) or image output (image model), and add small cached evals: photo extraction over a handful of real recipe photos (printed cookbook page, handwritten card, screenshot), and image generation over a few recipes, reviewed by eye. \
Changing only the text model while keeping a vision-capable one for photo extraction is fine if that is what the evals show.\n\
4. \
Update defaults, dev.env.example, and cli.env.example. \
The AI cache key includes the model, so stale cached responses won't leak through; the mock OpenRouter fixtures may need their model names updated.\n\
\n\
Also relevant: a 2026-07-28 prod job failed on an upstream Gemini rate limit (see p3-openrouter-finish-reason-error).",
